Hollow Moon -- a Werewolves-style game over UNIX stream sockets (asyncio)
=========================================================================
Files
  hollowcomm.py   the ONE communications library (Hub for the server, Client for players)
  moderator.py    game server / rules; runs as Linux user hw_mod
  player.py       interactive terminal client; run as your own player user
  bot.py          automatic player (same Client API) to fill the table
  setup_users.sh / teardown_users.sh   create/remove the Linux users and install to /opt/hollow

Requirements: Linux, Python 3.8+ (standard library only for the game itself), root for user setup.

Quick start (7 players)
  sudo ./setup_users.sh 7                 # users hw_mod, hw_alice, hw_bob, ...; installs to /opt/hollow
  sudo -u hw_mod python3 /opt/hollow/moderator.py --players 7 --night 30 --talk 40 --vote 20 #times can be changed as needed
  sudo -u hw_alice python3 /opt/hollow/player.py                       # terminals 1..N, one per player use any of the user's names
  sudo -u hw_carol python3 /opt/hollow/bot.py                          # use the bot script for other players if u dont want to play against yourself
  ...
  The game starts when --players have joined, or when >= --min-players (5) have typed /ready.
  Timers: --night 45 --talk 120 --vote 40 (seconds) by default if not explicitly changed when running moderator.  Add --seed N for a repeatable role deal.
  Type /help in a player terminal for the commands.  sudo ./teardown_users.sh removes everything.

Rules in one paragraph
  Night: wolves chat privately and /kill NAME (plurality; a tie means no kill); the seer /peek NAME
  sees "wolf / not wolf"; the healer /guard NAME (not the same person twice running; self once).
  Day: talk (public), /w NAME text (2 whispers; everyone learns THAT you whispered, not to whom),
  /ready to move on early, then /vote NAME|none with open ballots; plurality lynches. Roles are
  revealed on death.  Village wins when no wolves remain; wolves win when they equal the rest.

Reproduce the report's evidence
  sudo python3 demo/drive.py && python3 demo/render.py   # needs: pip install pexpect pyte playwright
  sudo bash demo/security_test.sh ; sudo bash demo/snapshot.sh
